Z||000005||iplayazi||04-14-2000||07:30 PM||||Is there much of a difference with a 88 gt rather 87??  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/confused.gif">  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/confused.gif">  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/confused.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000006||stimpy||04-14-2000||07:50 PM||||All beneath the skin... the 88 is really different as far as suspension bits go, but I will never stop loving my 86 GT!||||reg||1
Z||000007||Capt Fiero||04-14-2000||07:50 PM||||hmm 88 vs 87 88 had power lumbar adjustable seats.  88 had the best suspension of all Fiero's 88 had a carbon fiber look alike dash panels. mm everything on an 88 will cost you twice what it will cost on an 87, some 88 parts are no longer being made. Most suspension mods are for 84-87 not for 88.  It is a toss up, if you want a fiero to drive and just have fun buy an 88.  If you want a car that you can chop cut build modify and surpass the 88 buy an 84-87.  I personally love the idea of the 88 but I probably would would not buy one for the fact that I could build an 87GT that I would like for cheaper and easier than an 88.  Just try and find replacment 88 rear calipers. <BR>No flames I love all Fiero's just see the 88 to be harder to modify the way I like. ||||reg||6
